! mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap -- "THE COMMUNICATION REGION FOR MCP",
! printed page 103.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.110, header
! read and not assumed: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041
! PUNID 11011MCP   CARD ID CA000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01
! PAGE NUMBER 103".
!
! >>> A NEW PUNCHED DECK STARTS HERE, AND IT IS A SECOND COPY OF
! THE COMMUNICATION REGION. <<<  The card-serial column restarts at
! CA000001 (line 1) and runs to CA000056 (line 56) -- fifty-six
! lines, counted off the serial column, nothing lost off the top or
! the bottom of the render.  printed pp.97-98 were still punching
! 18xxxxxx serials.
!
! THIS PAGE IS printed p.37 ASSEMBLED AGAIN AT A NEW ORIGIN.  p.37
! is "THE COMMUNICATION REGION FOR MCP" at 002147.40..002166.40;
! this page lays the same region out at 215000.00..215021.00 with
! nineteen new SCOMRG bit definitions added and several values
! changed.  Twenty-six of its names are p.37's names to the letter
! (S MCP, S COM SZ, S COM RG, S XCHAN, S CHAN K, S CHANS, S BAMCP,
! S R TAPE, S W TAPE, S READ R, S BA PP, S MAXRN, S YCOCH, S YPRCH,
! S DKMCP, S SYRFT, S PR IN, S PR OUT, S IF DMP, S REJ JB, S ROOF,
! S MARK, S IA, S DATE, S TODAY, S END CM).
!
! >>> THE ORIGIN IS NOT SET ON THIS PAGE. <<<  There is no SLC row
! here.  printed p.99 line 11 is "SLC,(8)215000.", and nothing
! between there and here consumes storage, so the counter arrives
! at 215000.00 and line 6 is the first row to spend it.  CHECKED,
! NOT ASSUMED, for the two pages I had not been told about:
!   printed p.101 ("UNIT AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS") and printed p.102
!   ("FILE AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS") are SYN-only pages.  Every row
!   with a LOCATION prints a SYN VALUE with a trailing "+" relative
!   to a zero base -- 000000.14+, 000001.06+, 000010.40+ and so on
!   -- which is a resolved value and not the location counter, so
!   the counter does not move on either page.
!   printed p.100 ("MCP IOD CARDS") is comment cards only.
! The agreement is then two-sided: p.99's SLC says 215000 and THIS
! page's line 6 PRINTS 215000.00.
! The SLC written below is that origin, restated so the deck
! assembles standalone.
!
! >>> TWO KINDS OF ENTRY IN THE LOCATION COLUMN, AND ONLY ONE OF
! THEM IS AN ADDRESS. <<<  A row whose location ends in "+"
! (lines 10-27, 29, 30 and 51) is a SYN and the column prints its
! RESOLVED VALUE, not the counter; the counter does not move for
! it.  A row whose location has no "+" (lines 6, 7, 8, 28, 31-50
! and 53-56) is storage and the column is the real address.
!
! THE ADDRESS CHAIN CLOSES END TO END OVER THE SECOND KIND.
! FIRST printed address 215000.00 (line 6), LAST printed address
! 215020.40 (line 56); every storage row's printed address plus its
! own length equals the next storage row's printed address, with no
! gap and no overlap, across all twenty-eight of them.  Line 56 is
! a half word, so the counter reaches 215021.00 for whatever page
! follows.
!
! SEVEN COMMENT CARDS: lines 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 9 and 52.
!
! >>> THE "-" IN THE FLAG COLUMN IS NOT THE TELL, AND THIS PAGE
! DISPROVES IT. <<<  Measured at 1200 dpi: lines 1-5 and line 9 DO
! print a "-" in the one-character column between BINARY OUTPUT and
! NAME.  LINE 52 DOES NOT.  Line 52's column is blank and the
! hyphen one sees is the first character of the comment TEXT,
! "-IPL TENTACLE TABLE", printed out in the STATEMENT column.  That
! column is simply card column 2 of a RAW CARD IMAGE, and column 2
! holds a dash on some comment cards and a blank on others.
!
! THE TWO TELLS THAT HOLD FOR ALL SEVEN are:
!   (1) LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT are BOTH empty, and
!   (2) the card prints raw from column 2 on, so its fields do not
!       line up: the NAME column is empty on every one of them and
!       the text runs straight through from the STATEMENT column.
! Compare line 53, which looks crowded ("S IPL IN INDMK,4" with no
! gap) but is NOT a comment card: its name is eight characters and
! fills the field exactly, and it prints a LOCATION (215016.00) and
! a full word of BINARY.
!
! The seven read:
!   1  *********************************************************
!   2       ******** THE COMMUNICATION REGION FOR MCP ********
!   3  *********************************************************
!   4  THE FOLLOWING UP TO SIPL + 1.0 SHALL NOT BE MODIFIED UNDER ANY
!   5  CIRCUMSTANCE WITHOUT THE CONSENT OF THE IPL MAINTAINER........
!   9  19 BITS DEFINED FOR SCOMRG ARE BELOW.
!  52  -IPL TENTACLE TABLE
! Line 4 names SIPL, which is not defined on this page.
! S IPL IN's address is corroborated off the page: printed p.120
! line 2 prints "XS IPL IN" with the half word 215016.00+.
!
! >>> TWO LISTING MARKS, RECORDED AND NOT EXPLAINED. <<<  Line 7
! prints its line number as "7**" where every other row prints
! "N*", and line 7 is the only FORWARD reference on the page
! ("VF,SENDCM-SMCP", and S END CM is defined on line 51) -- printed
! p.37 line 9 is the same statement and carries the same "9**".
! Line 48 prints a bare "*" AFTER its location, "215013.40 *";
! p.37's line 29 and p.3 carry that mark too.  Neither changes a
! compiled bit and neither is checked here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 6    S MCP    VF,SMCP        -- the region's base, pointing at
!                                      itself: 215000.00.
! Line 7    S COM SZ VF,SENDCM-SMCP -- 000016.00, FOURTEEN WORDS, the
!                                      same size p.37 compiles.
! Line 8    S COM RG XW,(8)520000.  -- the system word.  p.37's is
!                                      XW,(8)100000.0 -- a DIFFERENT
!                                      flag pattern, read as printed.
! Lines 10-27  nineteen SYN(BU,1)/SYN(BU,2) bit definitions inside
!              S COM RG, bits 0..18 (the page's own line 9 says "19
!              BITS DEFINED FOR SCOMRG ARE BELOW" and there are
!              exactly nineteen bits once SYSMOD's two are counted).
! Line 28   S XCHAN  XW,0           -- channel status table base.
! Lines 29-30  its two SYN views (S CHAN K at +.28, S CHANS at +0).
! Lines 31-47  sixteen VF half words and one instruction: the I/O
!              reference numbers,
!              the console and printer channel numbers, the PRIME
!              routine entry and save slots, and the instruction-
!              fetch trap S IF DMP (line 43), which is the page's
!              ONLY instruction -- a BD, Branch Disabled, this time
!              not to 0 as on p.37 but to SDISIC+.32.
! Line 48   CNOP, to full-word-align the two date words.
! Lines 49-50  S DATE "03/15/63" and S TODAY "  /  /63", the same
!              two (AX) character words p.37 lines 42-43 carry.
! Line 51   S END CM SYN,$ -- the end of the region, 215016.00.
! Lines 53-56  the IPL TENTACLE TABLE: an INDMK indicator mask, a
!              zero word, S JCTWS and S TERMI.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS AND SPELLINGS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.  Every name here is six or fewer characters once the
!     blanks come out, and THAT IS LOAD-BEARING for one glyph: see
!     S HS ECH below.
! (2) Nothing else is substituted.  No printed spelling was rejected
!     by strap_asm except as recorded under ASSEMBLER LIMITATION.
!
! >>> THE 0/C GLYPH PAIR, AND HOW EACH ONE WAS SETTLED. <<<
! This page opens round glyphs everywhere -- its own column heading
! prints "LCCATICN" for LOCATION and line 5's comment prints
! "WITFOUT ... MCDIFIED".  Every round glyph in a LOCATION or an
! octal BINARY field is a 0 with certainty, because a C is not an
! octal digit: line 31's "2150CC.CC", line 35's "CCCCCC.CC+", line
! 53's "000000.CC CC" and line 54's bare-octal word all print 0 as
! an open C and every one is read as 0.
!
! The round glyphs that are NOT in an octal field are all in NAMES,
! and each was settled on something other than its shape:
!   * S HS ECH (line 11).  "ECH" could be a damaged "EXCH", which is
!     what "high speed exchange" would want.  IT CANNOT BE: names
!     are six or fewer characters once blanks are dropped (C22-6531
!     printed p.10), and S HS EXCH would be seven.  S HS ECH is six.
!     The comment "-HS ECH OPERATION BIT" prints the same three
!     letters, and printed p.153 line 42 prints
!     "CM1111(BU,1),S HS ECH" against 215001.01 -- another page
!     using the name, at THIS line's own address.
!   * S CNF CG (line 12) -- comment "-CONFIGURATION CHANGE FLAG",
!     so CNF = ConFiguration and CG = ChanGe.  Genuine C's.
!   * S CORG (line 13) -- comment "-COMPILE OR GO BIT", so C-OR-G.
!     Genuine C.  printed p.98 line 34 already carries S CORG.
!   * SLOCSU (line 26) -- printed "SLCCSU".  THE COMMENT IS NOT THE
!     ORACLE HERE ("-ON WHEN DISK IN SETUP" shares no letters), so
!     it was settled on ANOTHER PAGE: the listing prints
!     "Z DISKL BB,SLOCSU,$+2.0" against 215001.21 on printed p.152
!     line 7, with an O, and "CM0000,SLOCSU" against 215001.21 on
!     printed p.160.  Line 26's own address IS 215001.21, so those
!     rows and this one are the same symbol.  Read SLOCSU.
!     (Both witnesses were located in the OCR text and the glyph
!     was read there, NOT re-rendered -- weaker than the p.100
!     render above, and said so.)
!   * SYSMOD (line 18) -- the final glyph has the straight vertical
!     LEFT stem and squared corners of a D, not the round bowl of a
!     C or 0, and printed p.98 line 30 already carries SYSMOD.
!
! >>> ONE GLYPH NOT FULLY SETTLED: SJ1FUL (line 25). <<<  Grepping
! the whole listing for "FUL" -- deliberately NOT for "1FUL", since
! the OCR renders this very row's name as "SJLFUL" and a digit-
! keyed grep could not find a reference it had mangled the same way
! -- returns this row and nothing else.  So the name really does
! rest on ink: no other page uses it.  The second
! character is a digit 1 to the eye at 1200 dpi scaled 300% (it
! carries the top-left flag stroke that this drum's I does not), and
! the comment reads "-EQUALS ONE WHEN JC1 TABLES ARE FULL", which
! puts a 1 in the neighbourhood -- but the comment says JC1 and the
! name says J1, so the comment is NOT an exact oracle for it.
! Nothing else in the listing references the name, so it rests on
! ink.  SJIFUL with a letter I would assemble identically and
! listing_oracle could not tell them apart.  Recorded as uncertain.
!
! >>> WRITTEN DECIMAL, PRINTED OCTAL. <<<  Every SCOMRG bit offset
! is written decimal and prints octal: line 18 writes "+.8" and
! prints .10, line 19 writes "+.10" and prints .12, line 25 writes
! ".16" and prints .20, line 27 writes ".18" and prints .22.  Line
! 29 writes "+.28" and prints .34.  The (8) literals are the other
! way round and are written exactly as printed: line 37's
! "VF,(8)23.40" prints 000023.40+ and line 55's "VF,(8)42.0" prints
! 000042.00+.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHICH ROWS ARE INDEPENDENT CHECKS, AND WHICH ARE NOT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> EIGHT EXTERNAL SYMBOLS ARE SYNNED BELOW, AND SEVEN OF THEM
! CAME OFF ANOTHER PRINTED PAGE. <<<  No neighbouring page of this
! SECOND assembly has been transcribed into decks/ yet, so the
! witnesses are the listing itself on other printed pages rather
! than landed decks.  BE PRECISE ABOUT HOW EACH WAS READ: VRTP,
! VCRD and VWTP were found in docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt and
! then RE-RENDERED off the PDF at 900 dpi and read by eye, because
! the OCR mangled VRTP's value to "24-6".  The other four
! (SDISIC, SPRIME, SPRIMR, SIT) were read in the OCR text ONLY and
! were NOT re-rendered; each is corroborated by two to four
! separate OCR rows that agree digit for digit, which is why they
! are accepted, but they are a weaker class of evidence than the
! p.100 render and this deck does not pretend otherwise.
!   VRTP    000004.00  -- printed p.100 ("MCP IOD CARDS") prints the
!                         comment card "- VRTP   SYN,4." , rendered
!                         and read at 900 dpi, not taken from OCR.
!                         printed p.126 line 31 "RTABLE VF,VRTP"
!                         prints 000004.00+ as a second witness.
!   VCRD    000005.00  -- printed p.100's comment card "- VCRD
!                         SYN,5.", same render.  NOT a tautology.
!   VWTP    000006.00  -- printed p.100's "- VWTP   SYN,6."; printed
!                         p.126 line 32 "VF,VWTP" prints 000006.00+.
!   SDISIC  217451.40  -- the listing prints "SIC,SDISIC" with the
!                         operand half word "217451.40 80" on
!                         printed pp.119, 169, 173 and 193.  Line 43
!                         here writes SDISIC+.32 and prints
!                         217452.04, which is 217451.40 plus 32
!                         bits, so line 43 IS an independent check
!                         of the +.32 arithmetic and the BD encoding.
!   SPRIME  215570.00  -- printed p.132 "B,SPRIME" prints 215570.10
!                         and a plain B prints target+8 bits;
!                         printed p.193 prints it twice more.
!   SPRIMR  215571.00  -- printed pp.132 and 193 print "SIC,SPRIMR"
!                         as 215571.00 80.
!   SIT     215023.00  -- a LABEL in the LOCATION column on printed
!                         p.110 ("S IT  SIC,YMFIC" at 215023.00) and
!                         referenced as "SIT($4)" at 215023.00 on
!                         printed p.175.
!   ZFINIS  236464.00  -- BACK-DERIVED FROM LINE 56 OF THIS PAGE.
!                         It is the ONE tautological row here: no
!                         other row in the listing names ZFINIS.
!                         NOTE THE CONFLICT: decks/mcp_bootstrap_
!                         p98.strap carries ZFINIS at 017777.00 off
!                         printed p.98 line 31, which is the SAME
!                         statement "S TERMI VF,ZFINIS" in the FIRST
!                         assembly.  The two assemblies disagree and
!                         neither is wrong; see THE MERGE HAZARD.
! So twenty-five of the twenty-six checked rows are real checks and
! ONE (line 56) is a tautology.  The strongest rows are:
!   line  7  S COM SZ = SENDCM-SMCP = 000016.00, a fourteen-word
!            span this deck reproduces only if EVERY intervening
!            row's length is right -- it is the whole page's
!            counting in one number.
!   line 43  SDISIC+.32 -> 217452.04, address arithmetic across a
!            word boundary against an address read on four other
!            printed pages.
!   lines 6 and 31  SMCP -> 215000.00, this page's own origin.
! Lines 35, 36, 39, 40, 44, 45, 46, 48 and 54 name no symbol at all
! and check the encoding of VF, CNOP and DD alone.
!
! >>> THE MERGE HAZARD, WHICH IS NOT MINE TO FIX BUT MUST BE SAID.
! <<<  This page redefines, at new addresses, names that landed
! decks already define:
!     SMCP    002150.00 (pp.15/19/20/28/40)  ->  215000.00
!     SCOMRG  002151.00 (pp.31/33/98)        ->  215001.00
!     SXCHAN  002152.00 (p.37)               ->  215002.00
!     SYSMOD  002151.10 (p.98)               ->  215001.10
!     SCORG   002151.03 (p.98)               ->  215001.03
!     STERMI  005465.40 (p.98)               ->  215020.40
!     ZFINIS  017777.00 (p.98)               ->  236464.00
!     SPRIME  002166.00 (p.37)               ->  215570.00
!     SPRIMR  002166.40 (p.37)               ->  215571.00
!     and every other name p.37 defines.
! printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." starts a SECOND ASSEMBLY
! of MCP at a new origin; p.103 is its communication region.
! strap/mcp_image.py's merge() will see duplicate definitions the
! moment this page is added beside p.37 and p.98.  REPORTED, NOT
! TOUCHED -- nothing under strap/ was modified.

        SLC, (8)215000.0

! ---- externals, with the page each value was read on ---------------
VRTP    SYN, (8)4.0                  ! p.100 card; p.126 VF,VRTP
VWTP    SYN, (8)6.0                  ! p.100 card; p.126 VF,VWTP
VCRD    SYN, (8)5.0                  ! p.100 card "- VCRD SYN,5."
SPRIME  SYN, (8)215570.0             ! pp.132,193 "B,SPRIME" 215570.10
SPRIMR  SYN, (8)215571.0             ! pp.132,193 "SIC,SPRIMR" 215571.00
SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40            ! pp.119,169,173,193 "SIC,SDISIC"
SIT     SYN, (8)215023.0             ! p.110 label; p.175 SIT($4)
ZFINIS  SYN, (8)236464.0             ! ONLY line 56 here -- TAUTOLOGY

        SLC, (8)215000.0

! ---- the communication region --------------------------------------
SMCP    VF, SMCP                     ! line  6 -BASE ADDRESS OF MCP
SCOMSZ  VF, SENDCM-SMCP              ! line  7 -SIZE OF COMMUNICATION
                                      !           REGION
SCOMRG  XW, (8)520000.               ! line  8

! ---- the nineteen bits defined inside S COM RG ---------------------
SE      SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG            ! line 10
SHSECH  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.1         ! line 11 -HS ECH OPERATION BIT
SCNFCG  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.2         ! line 12 -CONFIGURATION CHANGE
                                      !           FLAG
SCORG   SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+0.03       ! line 13 -COMPILE OR GO BIT
SL      SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+0.04       ! line 14 -LEVEL OF INSTRUCTION
                                      !           COUNTER
SM      SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+0.05       ! line 15 -LEVEL OF INTERRUPT
SPINCL  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.6         ! line 16
SCSINT  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG.7          ! line 17
SYSMOD  SYN(BU,2), SCOMRG+.8         ! line 18 -TWO-BIT OPERATING MODE
STRANB  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.10        ! line 19
SSPFIX  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.11        ! line 20 -ON IF PP IN SPECIAL
                                      !           FIXUP
STSBIT  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.12        ! line 21 -ON IF TS STACKED FOR PP
SPPBT1  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.13        ! line 22 -3BITS FOR TRANSITION
                                      !           COMMANDS
SPPBT2  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.14        ! line 23
SPPBT3  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.15        ! line 24
SJ1FUL  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG.16         ! line 25 -EQUALS ONE WHEN JC1
                                      !           TABLES ARE FULL
SLOCSU  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG.17         ! line 26 -ON WHEN DISK IN SETUP
SJBUSY  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG.18         ! line 27

! ---- the channel status table --------------------------------------
SXCHAN  XW, 0                        ! line 28 -BASE ADDRESS OF CHANNEL
                                      !           STATUS TBLE.
SCHANK  SYN(BU,18), SXCHAN+.28       ! line 29 -NUMBER OF CHANNELS
                                      !           CONNECTED
SCHANS  SYN, SXCHAN                  ! line 30

! ---- the half-word slots -------------------------------------------
SBAMCP  VF, SMCP                     ! line 31
SRTAPE  VF, VRTP                     ! line 32
SWTAPE  VF, VWTP                     ! line 33
SREADR  VF, VCRD                     ! line 34 -INPUT SPOOL READER
                                      !           REF NO.
SBAPP   VF, 0                        ! line 35 -BASE ADDRESS OF THE PP
                                      !           I/O LOC TBL
SMAXRN  VF, 0                        ! line 36 -THE MAX. REF. NUMBER
                                      !           FOR A PP
SYCOCH  VF, (8)23.40                 ! line 37 -CONSOLE CHANNEL NUMBER
SYPRCH  VF, (8)22.40                 ! line 38 -PRINTER CHANNEL NUMBER
SDKMCP  VF, 0                        ! line 39 -MCP RESET TRACK FOR
                                      !           DISK
SSYRFT  VF, 0                        ! line 40 -VARIABLE POINTER FOR
                                      !           PP DISK ASSIGN
SPRIN   VF, SPRIME                   ! line 41 -ENTRY TO THE PRIME
                                      !           ROUTINE
SPROUT  VF, SPRIMR                   ! line 42 -SAVED ADDRESS OF JOES
                                      !           PRIME ROUTINE
SIFDMP  BD, SDISIC+.32               ! line 43
SREJJB  VF, 0                        ! line 44 -THE NUMBER OF JOBS TO
                                      !           REJECT
SROOF   VF, 0                        ! line 45
SMARK   VF                           ! line 46 -THE NEXT VACANT REEL
                                      !           SLOT FOR PP
SIA     VF, SIT                      ! line 47 -INTERRUPT TABLE ADDRESS
        CNOP                         ! line 48
SDATE   (AX)DD(BU),03/15/63X         ! line 49 - FOR DATE OF IPL TAPE
                                      !           TO SPOOL
STODAY  (AX)DD(BU),  /  /63X         ! line 50 -FOR DATE OF JOBS ON
                                      !           SPOOL TAPE
SENDCM  SYN, $                       ! line 51 -END OF COMMUNICATION
                                      !           REGION

! ---- the IPL tentacle table (line 52 is its heading card) ----------
! >>> THE PAGE PRINTS "INDMK,4" AND SO DOES THIS DECK NOW. <<<
! strap_asm had no INDMK and this row was written as a bit-identical
! DD(BU,64),(8)40000000000000000000 for one commit.  C28-6129 printed
! p.19 defines it -- "6. INDMK - Create one word of binary output ...
! producing one full word of binary output beginning at a full word
! address, with a bit pattern as specified in the address field, bits
! 0-63 ... e.g., INDMK, $ZM, $EXE, $IF" -- so INDMK,4 is one word with
! IBM BIT 4 set, i.e. 1 << 59, and nothing else.  strap_asm implements
! it now, including that document's own diagnostic 121, "BIT ADDRESSED
! TWICE IN LVS OR INDMK".  The printed spelling is restored.
SIPLIN  INDMK, 4                     ! line 53
                                      !          -USERBIT MCP
        DD(BU), 0                    ! line 54
SJCTWS  VF, (8)42.0                  ! line 55 - TWS FOR JC
STERMI  VF, ZFINIS                   ! line 56 -LAST MCP SLOT

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING -- every row with a LOCATION or BINARY entry.
! "BU,nn ,10" in the BINARY OUTPUT column of a SYN row is the DATA
! DESCRIPTION (mode BU, length nn octal, byte size 10 octal = 8),
! not machine code.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  6  215000.00   215000.00+                      S MCP    VF,SMCP
!   line  7**215000.40   000016.00+                      S COMSZ  VF,SENDCM-SMCP
!   line  8  215001.00   520000.00+ 000 000000 000000    SCOMRG   XW,(8)520000.
!   line 10  215001.00+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         S E      SYN(BU,1), S COM RG
!   line 11  215001.01+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         S HS ECH SYN(BU,1),S COM RG+.1
!   line 12  215001.02+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         S CNF CG SYN(BU,1),S COMRG+.2
!   line 13  215001.03+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         S CORG   SYN(BU,1), S COM RG + 0.03
!   line 14  215001.04+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         S L      SYN(BU,1), S COM RG + 0.04
!   line 15  215001.05+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         S M      SYN(BU,1),S COM RG+0.05
!   line 16  215001.06+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         S P INCL SYN(BU,1),S COMRG+.6
!   line 17  215001.07+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         S CS INT SYN(BU,1),S COM RG.7
!   line 18  215001.10+  +00000000     BU,02 ,10         SYSMOD   SYN(BU,2),SCOMRG+.8
!   line 19  215001.12+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         S TRAN B SYN(BU,1),S COM RG+.10
!   line 20  215001.13+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         SSPFIX   SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG+.11
!   line 21  215001.14+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         STSBIT   SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG+.12
!   line 22  215001.15+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         SPPBT1   SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG+.13
!   line 23  215001.16+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         SPPBT2   SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG+.14
!   line 24  215001.17+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         SPPBT3   SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG+.15
!   line 25  215001.20+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         SJ1FUL   SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG.16
!   line 26  215001.21+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         SLOCSU   SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG.17
!   line 27  215001.22+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10         S JBUSY  SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG.18
!   line 28  215002.00   000000.00+ 000 000000 000000    SXCHAN   XW,0
!   line 29  215002.34+  +00000000     BU,22 ,10         S CHAN K SYN(BU,18),S X CHAN+.28
!   line 30  215002.00+  +00000000     BU,100,10         S CHANS  SYN,SXCHAN
!   line 31  215003.00   215000.00+                      SBAMCP   VF,SMCP
!   line 32  215003.40   000004.00+                      SRTAPE   VF,VRTP
!   line 33  215004.00   000006.00+                      SWTAPE   VF,VWTP
!   line 34  215004.40   000005.00+                      S READR  VF,VCRD
